Acadex Teacher Flow — Liquid Glass Spec v1.0

Purpose: Finalize a deterministic, agent-executable UI flow for Teacher-side (including first-time onboarding) that adheres to the Liquid Glass aesthetic. This spec provides routes, component contracts, data-testid hooks, states, and acceptance criteria so another agentic system can implement the UI in one try.

⸻

1) Design Principles (Liquid Glass System)
	•	Aesthetic: translucent glass panels, soft depth blur, high-contrast text, subtle frosted edges, gentle motion (100–200ms), rounded (xl–2xl).
	•	Layout: responsive 1280–1536px optimal, grid-based cards, generous whitespace, focus on scan-ability.
	•	Tokens:
	•	Radius: --radius: 16px
	•	Elevation: --elev-1: 8px, --elev-2: 16px
	•	Blur: --blur: 20px
	•	Backdrop: --glass: rgba(255,255,255,0.12) on dark, rgba(0,0,0,0.06) on light
	•	Divider: rgba(255,255,255,0.18)
	•	Motion: --ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1); --dur: 160ms
	•	Iconography: Lucide set; stroke 1.5; rounded joins.
	•	Color/Grade mapping:
	•	Green A+–B- (#00C853 to #7CB342 gradient permitted)
	•	Yellow C+–D+ (#FFD600 to #FBC02D)
	•	Red < D+ (#FF5252 to #E53935)
	•	Use color bars/lozenges with accessible contrast (WCAG AA).

