5) Dashboard (Home)

Route: /dashboard

Header: “Class Overview” + + icon (Add Class) at top-right (data-testid="add-class").

Cards Grid: Each class card (data-testid="class-card") shows:
	•	Class Name (class-card-title)
	•	Total Students (class-card-students-count)
	•	Total Assignments (class-card-assignments-count)
	•	Average Grade (class-card-avg-grade + color badge)
	•	Click → /classes/:classId

Empty State: If no classes → glass card with CTA “Create your first class” (same add-class).

⸻

6) Add/Edit Class
	•	Add Button (global top-right or empty state) opens Create Class Modal (create-class-modal).
	•	Fields: class-name (required), class-description (optional), year-start, year-end.
	•	Primary: Create (create-class-submit), Secondary: Cancel.
	•	Edit via class context menu on Class Detail (optional MVP).

⸻

7) Class Detail

Route: /classes/:classId

Header: Class Name + Year Start–End display (class-year-range). Top-right: Create Assignment (add-assignment).

Assignments List (cards or list; default cards). Each Assignment Card (assignment-card):
	•	Title (assignment-title)
	•	Completion Rate: students complete / not complete (assignment-completion-rate)
	•	Grade Average (assignment-avg-grade + color)
	•	Click → /assignments/:assignmentId

Empty State: “No assignments yet. Create one.” with add-assignment CTA.

⸻

8) Assignment Creation Wizard (6 Steps)

Route: /classes/:classId/assignments/new or /onboarding/create-assignment

Progress Header: steps 1–6 with glass stepper (wizard-stepper).
	1.	Title (step1-title) – text input; required.
	2.	Assessment Details (step2-details) – rich text (or textarea) for instructions/outcomes.
	3.	Rubric (step3-rubric): Upload (rubric-upload) → parsed into editable textbox (rubric-editor).
	4.	Look Out For (step4-lookouts): 9 checkboxes (IDs fixed): big-ideas, grammar, student-thought-process, evidence-citation, structure, clarity, originality, analysis-depth, mechanics.
	5.	Grade Level (step5-gradelevel): Buttons K-6 (single), 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, College.
	6.	Grading Style (step6-style): Radio: critical, normal, flexible with descriptions.

Controls: Next (wizard-next), Back (wizard-back), Save & Exit (wizard-save-exit).

Validation: block Next if required fields empty. Auto-save draft every 10s.

⸻

9) Assignment Detail

Route: /assignments/:assignmentId

Header Metrics (glass stat chips):
	•	Average Grade (assign-avg-grade)
	•	Total Papers Uploaded (assign-total-uploaded)
	•	Total Papers Graded (assign-total-graded)

Primary Buttons (below metrics):
	•	Grade All (btn-grade-all) – filter dropdown: recent, year, all, past, present (grade-all-filter).
	•	Grade Checked (btn-grade-checked).
	•	Download Feedback (btn-download-feedback) – filter same as Grade All.

Submissions View (list default; toggle to cards):
	•	Each row/card (submission-row) shows:
	•	Checkbox (submission-check)
	•	Student-side logo if from student UI (submission-origin-logo) else none.
	•	Completion status icon: thumbs-up (green) or thumbs-down (grey/red) (submission-completion)
	•	Paper name (submission-title)
	•	Grade (submission-grade) + color pill per mapping
	•	3-dot menu (submission-menu):
	•	View Submission (menu-view)
	•	Evaluate this Paper (menu-evaluate)
	•	Edit Title (menu-edit)
	•	Download Paper (menu-download-paper)
	•	Download Grade Output (menu-download-grade)

Empty State: “No submissions yet.” with tips to upload or invite students (if Gold/School).

